@copilot this PR has review feedback that needs addressing:

- [#discussion_r3845670046](https://github.com/plengauer/Thoth/pull/4144#discussion_r3845670046) — the `case "$target" in */actions/instrument/deploy-local)` guard in the new `"Cleanup legacy .deploy-local artifact"` step (`actions/instrument/deploy/action.yml`, ~line 92) will not match the symlinks this PR is supposed to clean up, so the step silently does nothing. The legacy links were created with `ln -s "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/../deploy-local" "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/.deploy-local"` (see #4009), and `readlink` prints the raw, un-normalized target — e.g. `/home/runner/work/_actions/plengauer/Thoth/<ref>/actions/instrument/deploy/../deploy-local`. That string ends in `/deploy/../deploy-local`, which the pattern `*/actions/instrument/deploy-local` does not match (verified: the `case` falls through and no `rm` happens). Please make the guard match the target that is actually stored on disk — e.g. normalize the `deploy/..` segment out of `$target` before matching, or add patterns for `*/actions/instrument/deploy/../deploy-local` and the bare relative `actions/instrument/deploy-local` the reviewer mentioned, alongside the existing one. Keep the `[ -L "$path" ]` symlink check so an unrelated real file named `.deploy-local` is never removed. Ideally add a check that creates a symlink with the exact legacy target and asserts it gets removed, so this can't silently regress again.

